KUBERNETES DEPLOYMENT PAUSE, RESUME AND REPLICASET CLEANUP PRACTICAL

OBJECTIVE
1. Pause a Deployment rollout.
2. Apply multiple changes while rollout is paused.
3. Resume Deployment and trigger a single rollout.
4. Clean up old ReplicaSets using revisionHistoryLimit.

==================================================
STEP 1: CREATE DEPLOYMENT
==================================================

Create deployment.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: nginx-deploy
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:1.25

Apply:

kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml

Verify:

kubectl get deployment
kubectl get rs
kubectl get pods -o wide

==================================================
STEP 2: PAUSE DEPLOYMENT
==================================================

kubectl rollout pause deployment/nginx-deploy

Verify:

kubectl describe deployment nginx-deploy

Expected:
Deployment is paused

==================================================
STEP 3: UPDATE IMAGE
==================================================

kubectl set image deployment/nginx-deploy nginx=nginx:1.26

Verify:

kubectl get rs

Expected:
No new ReplicaSet is created.

==================================================
STEP 4: SCALE DEPLOYMENT
==================================================

kubectl scale deployment nginx-deploy --replicas=5

Verify:

kubectl get deployment

==================================================
STEP 5: ADD LABEL
==================================================

kubectl label deployment nginx-deploy env=prod

Verify:

kubectl get deployment --show-labels

==================================================
STEP 6: VERIFY NO ROLLOUT
==================================================

kubectl get rs

kubectl rollout history deployment/nginx-deploy

Expected:
Only original ReplicaSet exists.

==================================================
STEP 7: RESUME DEPLOYMENT
==================================================

kubectl rollout resume deployment/nginx-deploy

Monitor:

kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx-deploy

Verify:

kubectl get rs
kubectl get pods

Expected:
New ReplicaSet created with all changes.

==================================================
STEP 8: CREATE MULTIPLE REVISIONS
==================================================

kubectl set image deployment/nginx-deploy nginx=nginx:1.27
kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx-deploy

kubectl set image deployment/nginx-deploy nginx=nginx:1.28
kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx-deploy

kubectl set image deployment/nginx-deploy nginx=latest

Verify:

kubectl get rs

==================================================
STEP 9: CONFIGURE REPLICASET CLEANUP
==================================================

kubectl edit deployment nginx-deploy

Add:

revisionHistoryLimit: 2

Example:

spec:
  replicas: 5
  revisionHistoryLimit: 2

==================================================
STEP 10: TRIGGER ANOTHER ROLLOUT
==================================================

kubectl set image deployment/nginx-deploy nginx=1.29

kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx-deploy

==================================================
STEP 11: VERIFY CLEANUP
==================================================

kubectl get rs

Expected:
Only current ReplicaSet and last two old ReplicaSets remain.

==================================================
IMPORTANT COMMANDS
==================================================

kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
kubectl rollout pause deployment/nginx-deploy
kubectl rollout resume deployment/nginx-deploy
kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx-deploy
kubectl rollout history deployment/nginx-deploy
kubectl set image deployment/nginx-deploy nginx=nginx:1.26
kubectl scale deployment nginx-deploy --replicas=5
kubectl get rs
kubectl edit deployment nginx-deploy

==================================================
INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
==================================================

Q. Why pause a Deployment?
A. To apply multiple changes and create only one rollout.

Q. What happens when Deployment is paused?
A. Changes are stored but no new ReplicaSet is created.

Q. Why use revisionHistoryLimit?
A. To automatically delete old ReplicaSets and save resources.
